  <title>Customer payment</title>

  <p>Open <guiseq><gui>Customer</gui><gui>Customer payment</gui></guiseq>, the
  <gui>Customer Payment</gui> button of the main window, or <gui>Mark as
  paid</gui> in <link xref="unpaid_invoices"/>.</p>

  <steps>
    <item><p>Choose the customer in <gui>Contact</gui>. Their unpaid
    invoices are listed, oldest first.</p></item>
    <item><p>Choose how they paid: type the <gui>Check number</gui>, choose
    the account under <gui>Transfer to</gui> for a card or bank transfer, or
    choose <gui>Cash</gui>.</p></item>
    <item><p>Check the <gui>Date</gui> and type the <gui>Payment
    amount</gui>. Add a <gui>Comment</gui> if you like.</p></item>
    <item><p>Choose which invoices it pays, as below, and click <gui>Post
    payment</gui>.</p></item>
  </steps>
  <p>A check or cash payment waits in <link xref="deposits"/> until it is
  taken to the bank.</p>

  <section id="which_invoices">
  <title>Which invoices are paid</title>
  <p>With <gui>Apply payment to oldest invoice first</gui> checked, the
  payment and any earlier credit pay the invoices oldest first, for as many
  whole invoices as they cover. Selecting an invoice in the list unchecks it:
  then the selected invoices are the ones paid. Hold <key>Ctrl</key> to select
  several. <gui>Invoice totals</gui> shows what the selected invoices
  come to.</p>
  <p>Depending on <link xref="settings">the settings</link>, the
  payment either has to match the selected invoices exactly, and <gui>Post
  payment</gui> reads <gui>Totals do not match</gui> until it does, or it can
  differ, and <gui>The totals do not match !</gui> only warns you.</p>
  <p>The button also says what is missing: <gui>No contact selected</gui>,
  <gui>No check number</gui>, or <gui>No deposit account selected</gui>.
  Posting a payment of 0.00 asks first, since it is usually a mistake.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="discount">
  <title>Early payment discounts</title>
  <p>When the customer's <link xref="customer_terms">terms</link> give a
  discount for paying early, selecting one invoice shows the
  <gui>Discounted amount</gui> and the date it must be paid by. An invoice
  paid by then has its amount due lowered to the discounted amount; the
  difference is posted as a discount.</p>
  <p>To give a discount by hand, right click the invoice and choose
  <gui>Apply discount</gui>, then type what the invoice should come to. You
  can also type a lower <gui>Amount due</gui> straight into the list. Neither
  can raise an invoice above its total.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="cash_back">
  <title>Discounts and cash back</title>
  <p>Open <gui>Discounts / cashback</gui> to settle the invoices for a
  different amount than was paid, and type the difference in
  <gui>Amount</gui>:</p>
  <list>
    <item><p><em>Below zero</em> is a discount. The customer paid less, and
    you choose the expense account under <gui>Account</gui> that the shortfall
    is charged to. A check for 95.00 with <gui>Amount</gui> -5.00 settles 100.00
    of invoices.</p></item>
    <item><p><em>Above zero</em> is cash handed back. The customer paid more
    and got change, and you choose the cash account it came out of. A check for
    120.00 with <gui>Amount</gui> 20.00 settles 100.00 of invoices.</p></item>
  </list>
  <p>The payment then counts as the payment amount less the cash back, or plus
  the discount. That figure is the one matched against the invoices. It is
  also what statements, finance charges and the customer's balance show.
  <gui>Post payment</gui> reads <gui>No discount / cashback account</gui>
  until an account is chosen, and <gui>Parent account selected</gui> if the
  account has sub accounts. The check is still deposited for its full
  amount.</p>
  </section>

</page>
